{{/* Overall's body: the introduction and the sections, in djot, which overview.html places with {{body}}. */}}
::: intro
Overall, *Americans are wary of AI*{.finding}: they are far more concerned than excited; majorities say it's having negative impacts in their communities and making family life worse; and most see dealing with its harms as a priority for government action.

These views visibily shifted in the wake of two events: [OpenAI's disclosure in July](https://www.reuters.com/business/its-ai-agent-spent-days-hacking-company-sources-say-openai-did-not-notice-week-2026-07-24/) that two of its models had escaped their testing environment and hacked another company, Hugging Face, and [the resignation of an Anthropic employee, Jacob Coxon, in September](https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/anthropic-researcher-quits-over-out-of-control-ai-fears-707b7628).

Here are some key takeaways from our surveys so far:

- *Most Americans feel they have little say about AI in their lives.* Among all adults, {{.Share "inevitable" "008+009"}} say that AI is coming into their lives whether they want it or not, and {{.Share "can-shape" "008+009"}} say that people like them can shape it.
- *Concern rose after the Hugging Face disclosure.* The share of American adults who are excited about AI fell from {{.Share "excited" "002"}} to {{.Share "excited" "003"}}, and the very concerned share rose from {{.Share "very-concerned" "002"}} to {{.Share "very-concerned" "003"}}.
- *More Americans now say AI is already behaving in ways its developers did not intend.* Among all adults, {{.Share "already-unintended" "009"}} say that AI behaving in ways its developers did not intend is already happening, up from {{.Share "already-unintended" "001"}} in {{.When "001"}}.
- *The harms Americans most widely report are to job security and to knowing what's real.* Among all adults, {{.Share "worse-jobs" "008+009"}} say AI is making job security worse, and {{.Share "seeing-fake" "008+009"}} are seeing, or starting to see, people struggle to tell what's real from fake.
- *Most want the government to do more.* Among all adults, {{.Share "any-ai-harms" "008+009"}} call dealing with AI harms a top or important priority. On children and young people, {{.Share "little-children" "008+009"}} say that the government is doing too little and only {{.Share "much-children" "008+009"}} too much.

Our findings below draw on *{{text "basis" .}}*, which we break down in our [groups](groups/) page.

{{photo "driving.jpg" "A driver in a bucket hat at the wheel of a car, seen from the back seat" "@fujiphilm / Unsplash"}}
:::

{#personal}
## Personal Experience

Americans are *far more likely to be concerned than excited*{.finding} about AI's growing role in society.
Among all adults, {{.Share "concerned" "008+009"}} say they are concerned, including {{.Share "very-concerned" "008+009"}} who are very concerned.
In contrast, {{.Share "excited" "008+009"}} say they are excited.

{{chart "excited-or-concerned"}}

*Concern rose after Hugging Face*{.finding}, and has stayed higher since: from {{.Share "concerned" "002"}} in {{.When "002"}} to {{.Share "concerned" "003"}} in {{.When "003"}} and {{.Share "concerned" "009"}} in {{.When "009"}} ({{.Change "concerned" "002" "009"}}).

Concern also intensified after each event: those saying they are very concerned rose from {{.Share "very-concerned" "002"}} to {{.Share "very-concerned" "003"}} after Hugging Face ({{.Change "very-concerned" "002" "003"}}), and from {{.Share "very-concerned" "005"}} to {{.Share "very-concerned" "006"}} after Jacob Coxon's resignation ({{.Change "very-concerned" "005" "006"}}).

{{chart "concerned-over-time"}}

*Excitement fell after Hugging Face too, and has stayed lower*{.finding}: between the same two surveys, the excited share fell from {{.Share "excited" "002"}} to {{.Share "excited" "003"}} ({{.Change "excited" "002" "003"}}).

{{chart "excited-over-time"}}

*Most Americans say AI is coming into their lives whether they want it or not*{.finding}.
Among all adults, {{.Share "inevitable" "008+009"}} choose that statement, and {{.Share "can-shape" "008+009"}} say people like them can shape how much AI is part of their lives.

{{chart "ours-to-shape-or-inevitable"}}

